<item>
            <title>[IGNITE-4473] Client should re-try connection attempt in case of concurrent network failure</title>
                <link>https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IGNITE-4473</link>
                <project id="12315922" key="IGNITE">Ignite</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Problem&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br/&gt;
Consider the following scenario:&lt;br/&gt;
1) Client started, but there are no servers, so it hangs somewhere inside start routine.&lt;br/&gt;
2) Server appears, and discovery finishes successfully.&lt;br/&gt;
3) Nodes start talking to each other through communication SPI to finish start process (e.g. to complete exchange).&lt;br/&gt;
4) But network glitch occurs and server becomes unreachable.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Expected behavior&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br/&gt;
Client disconnects and hangs waiting for reconnect.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Actual behavior&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br/&gt;
Client throws an exception and never tries to reconnect.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
                <environment></environment>
        <key id="13030065">IGNITE-4473</key>
